const faq = [
  { q: 'Is an ace 1 or 11 in blackjack?', a: 'Either — whichever helps you more. A hand with an ace counted as 11 is called “soft”: ace-6 is soft 17. If a new card would bust you, the ace simply switches to 1.' },
  { q: 'What happens if you tie with the dealer?', a: 'It’s a push: you get your bet back and nobody wins. If you both have blackjack, that’s a push too.' },
  { q: 'How much does blackjack pay?', a: 'At a standard table a blackjack pays 3 to 2 — $15 on a $10 bet. Some tables pay only 6 to 5 ($12 on $10). That small change roughly quadruples the house edge, so avoid 6:5 tables.' },
  { q: 'When does the dealer have to hit?', a: 'The dealer has no choice: they hit on 16 or less and stand on 17 or more. At some tables the dealer also hits soft 17 (ace-6); the felt will say “Dealer hits soft 17” or “H17”.' },
  { q: 'Is blackjack the same as 21?', a: 'Blackjack is the casino version of the card game 21. The goal is the same, but in casino blackjack the dealer follows fixed rules and you get extra options like doubling, splitting and insurance.' },
];
---
<Guide
